A||||3||tomc||Do 1985 body parts interchange with 1986?
Z||000000||tomc||06-03-99||09:03 AM||||Does anybody have any insight on this? I've found a great deal on a 1985 parts car and need to replace my rear drivers side quarter panel on my 86GT. Will they switch?
Z||000001||Hock||06-03-99||11:27 AM||||Yes. Body parts from 84-86 are all interchangeable. 87-88 had a differant molding that went around the car.
Z||000002||GREENDANO||06-03-99||04:04 PM||||Remember a 86 GT upper rear 1/4 isn't the same as a notchback like the 85.  I just converted my 85 to a fastback like the 86-88's.  All the other body parts are the same.  I have an '88 fender and windshield from the local Pick-and-Pull.  Aren't they the greatest?  You're darn right I'll pay $30 for that windshield!!!<br>  Dan-O
Z||000003||ChadMan||06-04-99||10:12 AM||||My experience has been that nearly all body parts are interchangeable, though there are a few subtle differences among years.<p>For instance, I replaced a punctured door skin on my 1986 SE with a beautiful 1984 skin I found at a junkyard.  When I bolted it on, I discovered the little flaps at the top edge of the door had been changed somehow, so my door skin is only secured at the front, back, and bottom.  It looks good, but the top of the door skin flaps a bit at speeds over 100 mph.  :-)
